ccd/history/PROVENANCE: where the third-party material in ccrc history came from.

This is THIRD-PARTY CODE PROVENANCE, not release provenance: ccrc's own release
tarballs are attested and checked by deploy/verify-provenance.mjs and doctor's
`provenance` check, which never read this file. Everything listed here is
lossless-claw (Martian Engineering, MIT); its licence is LICENSE.lossless-claw,
byte for byte, in every directory that holds copied material.

One entry per copied item, entries separated by a blank line, six fields each:
  item             what was copied, with its harvest id (spec 2026-10-05 §11)
  ours             the repo-relative file that holds it now
  upstream         the upstream file's path inside lossless-claw
  commit           the upstream commit it was copied from
  upstream-sha256  sha256 of that whole upstream file at that commit
  changed          what this copy changed, or "nothing"
The file named by `ours` carries a one-line rationale comment of the form
"derived from lossless-claw <upstream> @ <commit>, MIT, see LICENSE.lossless-claw";
server/test/license.test.ts pins both directions.

